Change: Do not overwrite existing files by default during restore

The `restore` command now defaults to `--overwrite never` instead of
`--overwrite always`. Files that already exist at the target location are left
completely untouched, including their content, permissions and timestamps;
files that do not exist are still restored. The previous behavior is available
by explicitly passing `--overwrite always`.

This makes a restore into a non-empty directory safe by default, so an
accidental restore can no longer clobber existing data.

https://github.com/restic/restic/issues/22221
